## Relationships

### Parent Objective(s)

| Identifier | Title | Relationship |
|------------|-------|--------------|
| SO-F-001 | Provide Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence | Parent Objective |

SO-F-002 is directly derived from SO-F-001 and refines the root functional capability by establishing the system's environmental perception capability.

---

### Child Objective(s)

Child objectives shall be derived from SO-F-002 as the perception domain is decomposed.

Planned child objectives may include:

| Identifier | Title | Relationship |
|------------|-------|--------------|
| TBD | Acquire Environmental Information | Direct Child |
| TBD | Observe Vehicle State | Direct Child |
| TBD | Observe Human State | Direct Child |
| TBD | Detect Environmental Changes | Direct Child |
| TBD | Maintain Situational Observation | Direct Child |
| TBD | Assess Observation Quality | Direct Child |

These represent architectural intent only and are not yet approved objectives.

---

### Supporting Objective(s)

None at this stage.

Supporting relationships will be defined as additional objective categories (e.g., Safety, Coordination, Performance) are developed.

---

### Dependent Objective(s)

The following objectives are expected to depend on the successful realization of SO-F-002:

| Identifier | Title | Dependency |
|------------|-------|------------|
| SO-F-003 | Interpret the Operating Context | Direct Dependency |
| SO-F-004 | Generate Adaptive Decisions | Indirect Dependency |
| SO-F-005 | Execute Approved Actions | Indirect Dependency |

---

### Related Objective(s)

Relationships with objectives from other engineering domains will be established as those domains are created.

Examples include:

- Safety Objectives
- Coordination Objectives
- Performance Objectives
- Reliability Objectives

---

### Relationship Notes

SO-F-002 serves as the entry point of the operational capability chain within the Functional Objective hierarchy.

Changes to this objective may propagate through all downstream Functional Objectives that rely on environmental observations as the basis for adaptive behavior.
